  "worked_solution": "We multiply each entry of $G$ by $\\frac{1}{3}$ and each entry of $H$ by $2,$ and then add the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}G+2H & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 15 \\\\ -12 & 9 & 6\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 3 & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 6 & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 15 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-12) & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 9 & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 6\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot 1 & 2\\cdot 2 & 2\\cdot 5 \\\\ 2\\cdot 3 & 2\\cdot 4 & 2\\cdot 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 10 \\\\ 6 & 8 & 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+2 & 2+4 & 5+10 \\\\ -4+6 & 3+8 & 2+12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 11 & 14\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
